WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.526
Today is five letters. Two more round ones, and three that hook.

2
00:00:03.976 --> 00:00:10.788
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:11.288 --> 00:00:12.060
These five.

4
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.240
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

5
00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.860
This is the only letter that starts in the middle. Go across. Then curve back and around.

6
00:00:22.314 --> 00:00:26.789
This one starts high on the right. A little curve back. Then a little curve forward.

7
00:00:28.346 --> 00:00:33.384
This one hooks at the top. Curve over, pull down tall. Then lift, and go across.

8
00:00:34.902 --> 00:00:40.300
This one hooks at the bottom. Pull down below the line, and hook. Then lift, and add a dot.

9
00:00:41.651 --> 00:00:44.428
And this one: down, around, up, and down again.

10
00:00:45.886 --> 00:00:49.063
Your child finger-traces all five, saying each path.

11
00:00:49.513 --> 00:00:53.193
Then press play on the listening track for job two, and step away.

12
00:00:56.942 --> 00:00:57.880
The word is sun.

13
00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.825
In job three, your child traces the letters and writes the four words.

14
00:01:03.275 --> 00:01:10.939
If a day feels like too much, stop after the tracing. Do the rest tomorrow. Five careful letters beat fifty tired ones.

15
00:01:11.389 --> 00:01:15.238
At the end, they write two letters and one word while you watch the pencil.
